The steel sphere has a radius of $r = 3$ inches. The sphere is inscribed within a cube, meaning the diameter of the sphere is equal to the side length of the cube. The diameter of the sphere is $d = 2r = 2(3) = 6$ inches. Therefore, the side length of the cube is $s = 6$ inches.
The volume of the cube is given by $V = s^3$. Substituting $s = 6$, we get $V = 6^3 = 6 \times 6 \times 6 = 36 \times 6 = 216$ cubic inches.

\boxed{216}

