We want to find $\gcd(3339, 2961, 1491)$. First we find $\gcd(3339, 2961)$ using the Euclidean algorithm.
\begin{align*} 3339 &= 1 \cdot 2961 + 378 \\ 2961 &= 7 \cdot 378 + 315 \\ 378 &= 1 \cdot 315 + 63 \\ 315 &= 5 \cdot 63 + 0 \end{align*}
Thus, $\gcd(3339, 2961) = 63$. Now we compute $\gcd(63, 1491)$.
\begin{align*} 1491 &= 23 \cdot 63 + 42 \\ 63 &= 1 \cdot 42 + 21 \\ 42 &= 2 \cdot 21 + 0 \end{align*}
Therefore, $\gcd(63, 1491) = 21$. Thus, $\gcd(3339, 2961, 1491) = 21$.

